    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "In one day an elephant eats what a rabbit does in one year, taken to be 365 days. Together, in one day, they eat 100 kg of food. How many kilograms of food does the rabbit eat in one day?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{50}{183}\\text{ kg}$",
      "worked": "Let $r$ and $e$ be the amounts of food, in kilograms, eaten in one day by the rabbit and elephant respectively.\n$$\\begin{align*}e&=365r\\\\e+r&=100\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute $e=365r$ into the total-food equation.\n$$\\begin{align*}365r+r&=100\\\\366r&=100\\\\r&=\\frac{100}{366}\\\\r&=\\frac{50}{183}\\end{align*}$$\nThe rabbit eats $\\dfrac{50}{183}\\text{ kg}$ of food in one day.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 86
  },
